   "design": "One calendar view shows the judge's calendar, courtroom bookings and date rules together, instead of checking each separately. Counsel pick from offered slots on a scheduling form, instead of mail back and forth. The case management calendar holds hearings and deadlines, so the separate spreadsheet ends, and it prints the judge's daily schedule. Discussing with the judge, rooms and interpreters, entering appointments, checking and sending notices stay with the clerk. No model is used.",
   "previous_blocker": "Availability lived in several places and times were agreed by mail.",
   "enabler_now": "Combined calendar views, scheduling forms and printed schedules from the case system.",
   "still_hard": "Urgent hearings that displace others.",
   "human_edge": "Knowing which case the judge wants heard first.",
